  "deep_audit": true,
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "backproplab-stmt-1",
      "quote": "Backpropagation, introduced to the field of AI in \\citeyear{rumelhart1986}, is how a neural network **learns from its own mistakes**.",
      "block_id": "backproplab-block-1",
      "section": "",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-stmt-2",
      "quote": "**Forward Pass** — inputs flow *left → right* through the layers, producing a prediction.",
      "block_id": "backproplab-block-2",
      "section": "",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-stmt-3",
      "quote": "**Backward Pass** — the error flows *right → left*, telling each weight exactly how much to change.",
      "block_id": "backproplab-block-3",
      "section": "",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-stmt-4",
      "quote": "In the demo further down you can *watch* both flows as glowing pulses along the wires — each neuron's numbers update the instant a pulse lands on it.",
      "block_id": "backproplab-block-4",
      "section": "",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-stmt-5",
      "quote": "Click any neuron or weight to unfold its equations; every quantity wears an **underbrace** naming what it is in plain words, and a **show definition** toggle unfolds a symbol into its own formula.",
      "block_id": "backproplab-block-4",
      "section": "",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-stmt-6",
      "quote": "Instead of a toy 2‑2‑2 net, the demo below runs a **4-layer network** with shape **3 → 4 → 4 → 2**.",
      "block_id": "backproplab-block-6",
      "section": "The Network You'll Play With",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-stmt-7",
      "quote": "That's small enough to hand‑trace, deep enough to show how error signals *cascade* backward layer by layer — the exact behaviour that makes \"deep\" learning deep.",
      "block_id": "backproplab-block-6",
      "section": "The Network You'll Play With",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-stmt-8",
      "quote": "Each neuron does two things:",
      "block_id": "backproplab-block-8",
      "section": "One Neuron, In Slow Motion",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-stmt-9",
      "quote": "The **sigmoid** squashes any real number into $(0, 1)$.",
      "block_id": "backproplab-block-9",
      "section": "One Neuron, In Slow Motion",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-stmt-10",
      "quote": "Its derivative — which we'll need for backprop — is delightfully cheap once you already know $\\sigma(z)$:",
      "block_id": "backproplab-block-9",
      "section": "One Neuron, In Slow Motion",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-stmt-11",
      "quote": "Hover the plot below to see the tangent slope at any point:",
      "block_id": "backproplab-block-10",
      "section": "One Neuron, In Slow Motion",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-stmt-12",
      "quote": "We measure error with the **half sum-of-squares**:",
      "block_id": "backproplab-block-12",
      "section": "The Loss — \"How Wrong Are We?\"",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-stmt-13",
      "quote": "The $\\tfrac{1}{2}$ is a convenience — it cancels when we differentiate.",
      "block_id": "backproplab-block-13",
      "section": "The Loss — \"How Wrong Are We?\"",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-stmt-14",
      "quote": "(The standard **MSE** used elsewhere in the course is the same squared-error shape, averaged with $1/N$ instead of $\\tfrac12$.)",
      "block_id": "backproplab-block-13",
      "section": "The Loss — \"How Wrong Are We?\"",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-stmt-15",
      "quote": "Once you have $\\delta$ at a neuron, the gradient for any weight *feeding into* it is trivial:",
      "block_id": "backproplab-block-15",
      "section": "The Chain Rule Is All You Need",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-stmt-16",
      "quote": "And the update is a small step downhill:",
      "block_id": "backproplab-block-16",
      "section": "The Chain Rule Is All You Need",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-stmt-17",
      "quote": "where $\\eta$ is the **learning rate**.",
      "block_id": "backproplab-block-17",
      "section": "The Chain Rule Is All You Need",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-stmt-18",
      "quote": "**Press ▶ Forward** — watch cyan pulses travel left→right; each neuron's activation *updates the moment a pulse lands on it*.",
      "block_id": "backproplab-block-20",
      "section": "Now Watch It Happen",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-stmt-19",
      "quote": "**Press ◀ Backward** — watch red pulses travel right→left; each neuron's error signal $\\delta$ updates on arrival.",
      "block_id": "backproplab-block-21",
      "section": "Now Watch It Happen",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-stmt-20",
      "quote": "**Hover any neuron** — a *cone of influence* lights up every weight it touches, colored by that weight's contribution.",
      "block_id": "backproplab-block-22",
      "section": "Now Watch It Happen",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-stmt-21",
      "quote": "**Click any neuron or weight** — the panel below expands its full equations.",
      "block_id": "backproplab-block-23",
      "section": "Now Watch It Happen",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-stmt-22",
      "quote": "Every quantity wears an **underbrace** naming what it is, with a wider underbrace grouping related terms.",
      "block_id": "backproplab-block-23",
      "section": "Now Watch It Happen",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-stmt-23",
      "quote": "**Hit \"show definition\"** on a line — it unfolds that symbol into its own formula (e.g. the activation into the raw sigmoid).",
      "block_id": "backproplab-block-24",
      "section": "Now Watch It Happen",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-stmt-24",
      "quote": "**Press ✓ Full step**, then **↻ Train 100** — watch the values change on arrival and the loss bar shrink as the network adapts.",
      "block_id": "backproplab-block-25",
      "section": "Now Watch It Happen",
      "kind": "statement"
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "backproplab-block-1",
      "quote": "Backpropagation, introduced to the field of AI in \\citeyear{rumelhart1986}, is how a neural network **learns from its own mistakes**. It has two heartbeats:",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "section": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-block-2",
      "quote": "1. **Forward Pass** — inputs flow *left → right* through the layers, producing a prediction.",
      "kind": "list-item",
      "section": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-block-3",
      "quote": "2. **Backward Pass** — the error flows *right → left*, telling each weight exactly how much to change.",
      "kind": "list-item",
      "section": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-block-4",
      "quote": "In the demo further down you can *watch* both flows as glowing pulses along the wires — each neuron's numbers update the instant a pulse lands on it. Click any neuron or weight to unfold its equations; every quantity wears an **underbrace** naming what it is in plain words, and a **show definition** toggle unfolds a symbol into its own formula.",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "section": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-block-5",
      "quote": "The Network You'll Play With",
      "kind": "heading",
      "section": "The Network You'll Play With"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-block-6",
      "quote": "Instead of a toy 2‑2‑2 net, the demo below runs a **4-layer network** with shape **3 → 4 → 4 → 2**. That's small enough to hand‑trace, deep enough to show how error signals *cascade* backward layer by layer — the exact behaviour that makes \"deep\" learning deep.",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "section": "The Network You'll Play With"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-block-7",
      "quote": "One Neuron, In Slow Motion",
      "kind": "heading",
      "section": "One Neuron, In Slow Motion"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-block-8",
      "quote": "Each neuron does two things:",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "section": "One Neuron, In Slow Motion"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-block-9",
      "quote": "The **sigmoid** squashes any real number into $(0, 1)$. Its derivative — which we'll need for backprop — is delightfully cheap once you already know $\\sigma(z)$:",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "section": "One Neuron, In Slow Motion"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-block-10",
      "quote": "Hover the plot below to see the tangent slope at any point:",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "section": "One Neuron, In Slow Motion"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-block-11",
      "quote": "The Loss — \"How Wrong Are We?\"",
      "kind": "heading",
      "section": "The Loss — \"How Wrong Are We?\""
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-block-12",
      "quote": "We measure error with the **half sum-of-squares**:",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "section": "The Loss — \"How Wrong Are We?\""
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-block-13",
      "quote": "The $\\tfrac{1}{2}$ is a convenience — it cancels when we differentiate. (The standard **MSE** used elsewhere in the course is the same squared-error shape, averaged with $1/N$ instead of $\\tfrac12$.)",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "section": "The Loss — \"How Wrong Are We?\""
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-block-14",
      "quote": "The Chain Rule Is All You Need",
      "kind": "heading",
      "section": "The Chain Rule Is All You Need"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-block-15",
      "quote": "That's the whole trick. Once you have $\\delta$ at a neuron, the gradient for any weight *feeding into* it is trivial:",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "section": "The Chain Rule Is All You Need"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-block-16",
      "quote": "And the update is a small step downhill:",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "section": "The Chain Rule Is All You Need"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-block-17",
      "quote": "where $\\eta$ is the **learning rate**.",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "section": "The Chain Rule Is All You Need"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-block-18",
      "quote": "Now Watch It Happen",
      "kind": "heading",
      "section": "Now Watch It Happen"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-block-19",
      "quote": "Below is a live network. Try this in order:",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "section": "Now Watch It Happen"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-block-20",
      "quote": "1. **Press ▶ Forward** — watch cyan pulses travel left→right; each neuron's activation *updates the moment a pulse lands on it*.",
      "kind": "list-item",
      "section": "Now Watch It Happen"
    },
    {
      "id": "backproplab-block-21",
      "quote": "2. **Press ◀ Backward** — watch red pulses travel right→left; each neuron's error signal $\\delta$ updates on arrival.",
      "kind": "list-item",
      "section": "Now Watch It Happen"
    },
